kelixip (1.8.0-1) stable; urgency=low

  * A SpeechProcessor between the legs of a call (`speech:` in the media
    tuple): what one leg says is written to the other as T.140, what it types
    is spoken to the other. Audio and text go through it, video stays direct.
    Text goes through it on whichever leg carries it, so a callee without text
    still has its voice captioned.
  * A voice dialogue with a caller: start_speech, say, stop_speaking and
    stop_speech, with the voices read from speech-server.
  * Reference script call-captioning.exs: a challenged call relayed through
    the sip-trunk-prod trunk with audio and text only, AMR-WB then PCMA, the
    callee's voice captioned and the caller's typing spoken; 488 when the
    caller offers no text.
  * AMR-WB joins the codec vocabulary.
  * A conference that places a call without codec_order offers audio as OPUS,
    AMR-WB, SPEEX, G722, PCMA, PCMU, instead of in alphabetical order.
  * The SpeechProcessor and AMR-WB on the wire need mediaserver 1.19.0.
  * User-Agent is now Kelixip/1.8.0.

 -- Emmanuel BUU <emmanuel.buu@ives.fr>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:23:31 +0200

kelixip (1.7.1-1) stable; urgency=low

  * 1.7.0 together with everything delivered in 1.6.4-2 to 1.6.4-8: the
    kelixip-mod-sip-servers package (trunks, proxies and application servers,
    OPTIONS liveness, tertiary_uri, source_networks, use_fqdn_contact,
    publish_contact_host, ext_domain), the client certificate of config.toml
    [tls], the registration binding's User-Agent, Call-ID and CSeq, the PUBLISH
    received_time, trust_asserted_identity/1 and the SHA-256 digest spelling.
  * And everything delivered in 1.6.5-1 to 1.6.5-5: a P-Asserted-Identity
    holding two bracketed values on one line is refused instead of raising
    (Teams Direct Routing), the 2xx names the remote tag of an outbound
    dialog, a conference places calls (mcu dial_out/4, sip_servers
    dial_target/3), admit/3 takes the conference number (did:), a script
    starts on demand (POST /scripts/<name>/run, kelictl run), a trunk's
    keepalive OPTIONS comes from its account with a user part in its Contact,
    no module sends outbound SIP before the listeners are bound, and
    compile_and_restart_all keeps the installed distribution cookie.
  * User-Agent is now Kelixip/1.7.1.

